  "id": "visual-impairment",
  "term": "visual impairment",
  "definition": "Visual impairment is reduced sharpness of vision or loss of part of the visual field that limits a person’s ability to take in visual information. It can affect development and everyday functioning, including communication, learning, and social interaction.",
